[{:adr/authoritative_for ["opens Phase 1 (GTG field equations) as a deliberate, scoped exception to\n    ADR-2607051500/ADR-2607101700's 'action principle and field equations out\n    of scope' boundary -- narrowly for the source-free Omega-field equation of\n    motion (GTG's vanishing-torsion / first-Cartan-structure-equation analogue)\n    and, contingent on that, the true LDG linear curvature scalar" "context: Phase 0d (PR #7) and Phase 0e (PR #8) independently hit the same\n    wall from different angles while chasing the curvature scalar -- Phase 0d\n    found unresolved index/sign risk translating R_munu into a scalar; Phase 0e\n    found there is NO h_mu(x)->Omega_mu(x) correspondence anywhere in this\n    codebase (GTG's h is not an ordinary-GR tetrad, both indices live in the\n    same flat background space, tetrad-postulate formula does not transfer\n    verbatim). Root cause: h and Omega are independent gauge potentials in GTG\n    by construction; their relation only appears as the equation of motion from\n    varying the action w.r.t. Omega -- unreachable without touching the action\n    principle" "Phase 1 scope: (1) GTG gravitational action, vacuum/source-free only, no\n    matter coupling/cosmological-constant/Yang-Mills-Dirac-Higgs terms folded\n    in; (2) the Omega-field equation of motion from varying that action w.r.t.\n    Omega, giving Omega algebraically in terms of h and its derivatives in the\n    source-free case; (3) only after (1)-(2) land with independent numeric\n    verification, revisit the true curvature scalar R" "explicitly STILL out of scope, unchanged: matter coupling to gravity, the\n    Einstein multivector/stress-energy sourcing, any GR-equivalence proof (cited\n    as established 1998 literature result, not re-derived), quantization/RGE/\n    scattering/lattice, dark-sector/de-Sitter extension -- Phase 1 is bounded to\n    source-free Omega(h) + contingent curvature scalar only" "verification bar for any Phase 1 PR (given PR #6's real slot-order bug and\n    Phase 0d/0e's honest declines on exactly this class of derivation): at least\n    2 independent mutually-corroborating primary/secondary literature sources\n    for the exact equation, AND a genuine independent numeric check (reproduce a\n    literature worked example, or cross-check against linearized-GR\n    vanishing-torsion in a simple case) -- not merely 'the formula matches the\n    PDF on one read'. If the bar cannot be cleared, the correct outcome is\n    another honest non-implementation writeup (same as Phase 0d/0e), not a\n    lowered bar" "this ADR changes no code by itself -- a follow-up landing-record ADR should\n    document what actually merges, mirroring the ADR-2607101700 ->\n    ADR-2607101900 scope-then-landing pattern; if Phase 1 succeeds it would be\n    the first genuine GTG FIELD EQUATION (not just field-content algebra) in\n    this repo, a qualitative change from every prior ADR's framing that should\n    be revisited explicitly in the landing ADR, not left stale" "if Phase 1 fails to clear the verification bar (a live possibility -- two\n    prior adjacent-angle attempts both failed), the curvature-scalar chase\n    should not be reopened a further time without a materially new approach\n    (literature worked-example cross-check, independent expert consultation),\n    not another literature re-read"], :adr/supersedes [], :adr/superseded_by [], :adr/topic "kotoba-lang-standard-model", :adr/related ["adr-2607101900" "adr-2607101700" "adr-2607051500"], :adr/status "accepted", :adr/id "adr-2607102300-kotoba-lang-standard-model-gtg-phase1-field-equations-scope", :adr/doc_type "adr", :adr/last_verified "2026-07-09", :adr/body "see 2607102300-kotoba-lang-standard-model-gtg-phase1-field-equations-scope.md", :adr/deciders ["Jun Kawasaki"], :adr/date "2026-07-09", :db/id -1, :adr/authoritative true, :adr/title "ADR-2607102300: kotoba-lang/standard-model — opening Phase 1 (GTG field equations / the h-Omega relation), superseding the action-principle-out-of-scope boundary for this one item"}]